                        "translation_id": "a9816a71-fb10-4353-bb6b-70c3b7ee661a",
                        "source_entry_id": "4132d912-07d0-3949-8588-a1e7473b486a",
                        "source_sense_id": "3115dfc2-6e99-38dd-b453-168285abd94a",
                        "target_lang_word": "miscarry",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "miscarry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f38f9b54-2e31-3395-875c-c4652bbb3032",
                                        "entry_id": "a9f88531-a4ae-39dc-88a3-13197a3b60db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To have an unfortunate accident of some kind; to be killed, or come to harm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4747a39-cb99-31b0-bb4e-6083a9bbccb4",
                                        "entry_id": "a9f88531-a4ae-39dc-88a3-13197a3b60db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To go astray; to do something wrong."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24f78d87-5471-375f-8dd6-52112f87d88a",
                                        "entry_id": "a9f88531-a4ae-39dc-88a3-13197a3b60db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To have a miscarriage; to involuntarily abort a foetus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f26f3c04-78c3-349f-81b9-22511553fffc",
                                        "entry_id": "a9f88531-a4ae-39dc-88a3-13197a3b60db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fail to achieve some purpose; to be unsuccessful, to go wrong (of a business, project etc.)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6a4e3b6-d743-4e44-88b3-5a5e55c8e3ae",
                                                "sense_id": "f26f3c04-78c3-349f-81b9-22511553fffc",
                                                "text": "So, if a Sonne that is by his Father ſent about Merchandize, doe ſinfully miſcarry vpon the Sea; the imputation of his vvickedneſſe, by your rule, ſhould be impoſed vpon his Father that ſent him: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "701c61a1-4784-4dca-a04e-a7543a498b03",
                                                "sense_id": "f26f3c04-78c3-349f-81b9-22511553fffc",
                                                "text": "Pluto observing, since the Peace,\nThe Burial Article decrease;\nAnd, vext to see Affairs miscarry,\nDeclar'd in Council, Death must marry […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6676eff-10cb-39ec-adfc-d3cd632838e7",
                                        "entry_id": "a9f88531-a4ae-39dc-88a3-13197a3b60db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a letter etc.: to fail to reach its intended recipient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9281bb5-e3f0-4d1a-8fde-53003e4fd02a",
                                                "sense_id": "e6676eff-10cb-39ec-adfc-d3cd632838e7",
                                                "text": "Sir Nathaniel, this Biron is one of the votaries with the king; and here he hath framed a letter to a sequent of the stranger queen's, which accidentally, or by the way of progression, hath miscarried."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "168c59b1-773d-4f10-a72e-9d239ecdf949",
                                                "sense_id": "e6676eff-10cb-39ec-adfc-d3cd632838e7",
                                                "text": "It likewise alluded to several letters, which, as it appeared to me, must have miscarried or have been intercepted,[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb196ed5-75a6-4d83-8baf-c98d191f733d",
                                                "sense_id": "e6676eff-10cb-39ec-adfc-d3cd632838e7",
                                                "text": "Since the luckless Friday morning he had neither been seen nor heard of; day after day, Adeline had trusted to receive a letter, but in those times posts were slow and uncertain, messengers and couriers were often employed instead; and the hope might reasonably be clung to of a letter having miscarried."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
